---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_67",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 67,
  "text": "[[180.1]] <b>55.  Quid sit natura prius [Frühjahr bis Sommer 1679 (?)]</b>\n [[180.2]] <tab/>[Frühjahr bis Sommer 1679 (?)] </p>\n<p> [[180.12]] Difficultas aliqua est in explicando quid sit <b>natura prius</b>. Nam ut status posterior\n[[180.13]] alicujus substantiae involvit priorem, ita vicissim status prior involvit ­posteriorem,\n[[180.14]] unusquisque enim ex alio potest cognosci. Unde sequi videtur, priorem non esse simpliciorem\n[[180.15]] posteriore sed ambos eadem involvere, et aequationem quandam intercedere.\n[[180.16]] Sed videtur solutio difficultatis exemplo eleganti illustrari posse, constat plures saepe\n[[180.17]] esse proprietates ejusdem subjecti, quarum una altera facilior inventu demonstratuque est,\n[[180.18]] et tamen omnes sunt reciprocae, adeoque eadem omnia involvunt. Sic prior et simplicior\n[[180.19]] est circuli proprietas, [sinum] esse mediam proportionalem inter segmenta\n[[180.20]] diametri, quam rectis se in circulo decussantibus rectangula segmentorum\n[[180.21]] compertinentium utrinque aequalia esse, atque adeo et natura prior, etsi\n[[180.22]] haec ut genus illam comprehendat; nam in analogis species genere prior.\n[[180.23]] Et proprietas segmentorum generalis est ex numero perplexarum seu paradoxarum, quarum\n[[180.24]] possibilitas potest dubitari, itaque si quaeratur linea talis naturae, dubitari potest an\n[[180.25]] possibilis sit ejus solutio. Sic facilius demonstratur circulum in suo segmento eundem\n[[180.26]] angulum ubique capere, quam circulum esse capacissimam figurarum isoperimetrarum.\n[[180.27]] Eodem igitur modo duo status universi, etsi alter alterum involvat non aeque tamen facile\n[[180.28]] intelliguntur, et ex fontibus explicantur. </p>\n<p> [[181.1]] Et proinde <b>Natura prius</b> est, cujus possibilitas facilius demonstratur; seu quod\n[[181.2]] facilius intelligitur. Ex duobus statibus quorum alter alteri contradicit, is est <b>tempore\n[[181.3]] prior</i>, qui est prior natura. Duo existentia incompatibilia seu contradicentia tempore\n[[181.4]] differunt, et illud prius est aut posterius tempore, quod est prius aut posterius natura. </p>\n<p> [[181.5]] In natura, ut in arte tempore priora sunt simpliciora, posteriora sunt perfectiora. Nam\n[[181.6]] natura est ars summa. Haec propositio magni momenti est, et contra regressum in orbem,\n[[181.7]] ubi nullus finis. Ut felicitas in progressu ulteriore sic et rerum perfectio, ut quam\n[[181.8]] directissime in perfectione crescant. Nihil unquam in creaturis perfectissimum. </p>\n",
  "number": "55.",
  "title": "Quid sit natura prius",
  "date": "[Frühjahr bis Sommer 1679 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:55. Quid sit natura prius [Frühjahr bis Sommer 1679 (?)] [Frühjahr bis Sommer 1679 (?)] Difficultas aliqua est in explicando quid sit natura prius. Nam ut status posterior alicujus substantiae involvit priorem, ita vicissim status prior involvit ­posteriorem, unusquisque enim ex alio potest cognosci...">
      <div class="text-content">
        {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
          paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>